    <briefdescription>
<para>Hash set of interned variable-size monomials <mdash/> the variable-length counterpart of <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_set_fixed_size" kindref="compound">MonomialSetFixedSize</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Each monomial is a contiguous range <computeroutput>[m, m + *m)</computeroutput> where the leading int is the length, so the set itself stores only <computeroutput>const int*</computeroutput> pointers; the storage is owned by the caller (typically a <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_memory_space" kindref="compound">MonomialMemorySpace</ref></computeroutput>). <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_set_var_size_ab42353083cc023b53387e1a6b9999df1_1ab42353083cc023b53387e1a6b9999df1" kindref="member">findOrInsert</ref></computeroutput> returns the canonical pointer plus a flag indicating whether a new entry was created. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
